From 87b3aaa3cb98f20f41a24305443f07c9c5d9b4b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:44:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat waits: a 2 h board deadline and a daily
 cap end every unanswered ask

Review and adversarial pass of the previous head:
- A wake the sweeper tried but that did not start (refused, error, busy,
  missing) still acked the ask as a passive row with no escalation. Instead of
  patching each delivery path, the guarantee now sits on the board: after the
  card's own comment probe says "not yet", kanban_wake_check calls
  kanban_decision_ask.escalate_if_overdue, and a chat park older than
  ASK_OVERDUE_S (2 h) with no answer goes to David (needs_input). escalate()
  re-checks for an answer first, so an answer that beat the deadline wins.
- "Not yet" replies reset the streak forever: CHAT_PARK_CAP (6) chat parks per
  card per 24 h escalate however each was answered.
- The card's own worker commenting before it re-asks counted as an answer:
  _answered_since ignores comments stamped with one of this card's runs.
- Sweeper: a failing escalation is logged, not swallowed; after escalating it
  acks the claim without writing the now-stale "parked until you decide" row.

Tests: the 2 h backstop (and an answer beating it), the wake-check runner
calling it after a "not yet", six "not yet" answers then escalation, the
worker's own notes not counting. 5 of 60 fail on the previous head; 31
neighbouring files (647 tests) pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
